    {
      "body": "### ROCm results for this batch (per-test) — why it was closed\n\nSource: `jit-kernel-unit-test-amd-rocm720` run [28768600693](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/28768600693) (MI325 / gfx942, `continue_on_error` so every file ran).\n\n| Test | Result | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_concat_mla.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: `concat_mla.cuh` includes `cuda_bf16.h` |\n| `test_set_mla_kv_buffer.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: `set_mla_kv_buffer.cuh` includes `cuda/ptx` |\n| `test_hadamard_jit.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: hadamard kernel includes `cuda_bf16.h` |\n| `test_timestep_embedding.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: `timestep_embedding.cuh` includes `cuda_runtime.h` |\n| `test_moe_lora_align_block_size.py` | ❌ fail | CUDA-only kernel: `moe_lora_align_kernel.cu` includes `cub/cub.cuh` |\n| `test_per_token_group_quant_8bit.py` | ❌ fail | Compiles on ROCm; fp8 `float8_e4m3fn` TensorMatcher mismatch (functional gap, potentially fixable) |\n| `test_per_tensor_quant_fp8.py` | ❌ fail | Same fp8 `e4m3fn` category (compiles; functional gap) |\n| `test_moe_fused_gate.py` | ❌ fail | Fails to compile on ROCm (exact blocking include not cleanly captured) |\n\n**Outcome:** 0/8 are ROCm-portable, so this PR was **closed** (superseded by #30212). The CUDA-only kernels are tracked for dashboard exclusion in ROCm/sglang-ci#297. The fp8 quant tests (`per_token_group_quant_8bit`, `per_tensor_quant_fp8`) are a genuine, potentially-fixable gap (e4m3fn vs fnuz on ROCm) and were intentionally **not** marked NV-only.",
